"<p>Nitrobase collects server and container telemetry directly over SSH or local host execution—no external Prometheus, Grafana, or host agents required.</p>\n<h2>Server &#x26; Container Monitoring</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Collection loop:</strong> Polls every Ready server every <code>15s</code> (<code>MONITORING_INTERVAL_MS</code>, toggleable with <code>MONITORING_ENABLED=true</code>) for CPU, load average, memory, swap, disk usage, network I/O, and per-container stats/status.</li>\n<li><strong>Retention &#x26; rollups:</strong> Raw samples are kept for <code>24</code> hours (<code>METRICS_RAW_RETENTION_HOURS</code>) and rolled up into <code>5</code>-minute buckets kept for <code>7</code> days (<code>METRICS_ROLLUP_RETENTION_DAYS</code>), powering <code>1h</code>, <code>24h</code>, and <code>7d</code> history charts.</li>\n<li><strong>Built-in alert rules:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Disk usage:</strong> Opens at <code>85%</code> (<code>ALERT_DISK_PERCENT</code>), resolves below <code>80%</code> (<code>ALERT_HYSTERESIS_PERCENT=5</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Memory usage:</strong> Opens at <code>90%</code> (<code>ALERT_MEMORY_PERCENT</code>), resolves below <code>85%</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Restart loops:</strong> Triggers when a container restarts <code>3</code> times within <code>10</code> minutes (<code>ALERT_RESTART_LOOP_COUNT</code>, <code>ALERT_RESTART_LOOP_WINDOW_MINUTES</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>OOM kills &#x26; stopped services:</strong> Detected directly from container inspection.</li>\n<li><strong>Server unreachable:</strong> Triggers after <code>3</code> consecutive failed ticks (<code>ALERT_UNREACHABLE_FAILURES</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Proxy network self-heal:</strong> Automatically repairs containers detached from <code>nitrobase-network</code>, or raises a <code>network_flap</code> alert after <code>3</code> consecutive repair attempts (<code>NETWORK_REPAIR_MAX_ATTEMPTS</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Live Container Logs</h2>\n<p>Stream real-time container stdout/stderr in the browser (<code>/api/apps/&#x3C;appId>/logs</code>) or fetch masked tails via the REST API / MCP server (<code>POST /api/v1/apps/{appId}/logs</code>). Secret values are automatically redacted before leaving the server. Up to <code>4</code> concurrent log streams per user (<code>APP_LOG_STREAMS_PER_USER</code>) are supported.</p>\n<h2>Interactive Web Terminal</h2>\n<p>Open a full interactive PTY terminal powered by <strong>xterm.js</strong> over WebSockets:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Server terminal</strong> (<code>server.terminal</code> permission): Shell access directly on a managed VPS or Localhost.</li>\n<li><strong>Container terminal</strong> (<code>app.terminal</code> permission): Interactive <code>docker exec</code> shell inside any running app container.</li>\n<li><strong>Security:</strong> Sessions revalidate every <code>30s</code> (<code>SESSION_REVALIDATE_INTERVAL_MS</code>), close immediately if the user's session is revoked, disconnect after <code>30</code> minutes of inactivity (<code>TERMINAL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS</code>), and are recorded in the audit log.</li>\n</ul>"